{"id":"CVE-2009-3703","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2009-12-18T19:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T06:38:30.209Z","description":"Multiple SQL injection vulnerabilities in the WP-Forum plugin before 2.4 for WordPress allow remote attackers to execute arbitrary SQL commands via (1) the search_max parameter in a search action to the default URI, related to wpf.class.php; (2) the forum parameter to an unspecified component, related to wpf.class.php; (3) the topic parameter in a viewforum action to the default URI, related to the remove_topic function in wpf.class.php; or the id parameter in a (4) editpost or (5) viewtopic action to the default URI, related to wpf-post.php.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/37357","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"37357"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/archive/1/508504/100/0/threaded","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_BUGTRAQ"],"name":"20091216 [ISecAuditors Security Advisories] WP-Forum <= 2.3 SQL Injection vulnerabilities"}],"exploitdb":[{"edb":"10488","title":"WordPress Plugin WP-Forum 2.3 - SQL Injection / Blind SQL Injection","type":"webapps","platform":"php","date":"2009-12-16","verified":"1"}],"vendors":["wordpress"]}
